@startuml
' Figure 2.2 – Class diagram: core domain
' The accounts, the articles and their social layer, with the enumerations
' they reference. Audit columns (created_at, updated_at) are omitted.
'
' Operations are the domain operations each class supports, named after the
' service methods that implement them (articles.service, comments.service,
' auth.service, subscriptions.service, moderation.service…): the behaviour
' lives in the service layer, the diagram shows which class it belongs to.
'
' Like, Repost, Save, CommentLike, Follow and Block carry nothing but the pair
' they join and a date, so they are drawn as many-to-many associations rather
' than classes. Each is a join table in the physical schema, with a unique
' constraint on its pair.
!include ../_style.puml
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 55
hide circle
hide empty methods

class User {
  - id : UUID
  - accountType : AccountType
  - email : String
  - username : String
  - role : Role
  - plan : Plan
  - earningsBalance : Integer
  - isMarketplaceEligible : Boolean
  - aiTokensRemaining : Integer
  - deletedAt : Timestamp
  + register()
  + signIn()
  + updateProfile()
  + setPlan(plan : Plan)
  + like(article : Article)
  + unlike(article : Article)
  + repost(article : Article)
  + save(article : Article)
  + follow(user : User)
  + block(user : User)
  + likeComment(comment : Comment)
}
class MagazineProfile {
  - displayName : String
  - slug : String
  - subscriptionStatus : SubscriptionStatus
  - creditBalance : Integer
  - monthlyCreditAllowance : Integer
  - subscriptionExpiresAt : Timestamp
  + subscribe()
  + topUp(credits : Integer)
  + cancel()
}
class Article {
  - id : UUID
  - publisherId : UUID
  - title : String
  - slug : String
  - content : Json
  - contentSearch : TsVector
  - status : ArticleStatus
  - placement : Placement
  - visibility : Visibility
  - marketplacePrice : Integer
  - wordCount : Integer
  - publishedAt : Timestamp
  - deletedAt : Timestamp
  + update()
  + publish(placement : Placement, visibility : Visibility)
  + switchToPublic()
  + softDelete()
}
class Tag {
  - name : String
  - slug : String
  + findAll() : Tag[]
  + create(name : String)
}
class Comment {
  - content : Text
  - deletedAt : Timestamp
  + reply(content : Text) : Comment
  + remove()
}
class Notification {
  - type : NotificationType
  - data : Json
  - isRead : Boolean
  + markRead()
}
class Report {
  - targetType : ReportTargetType
  - targetId : UUID
  - reason : Text
  - status : ReportStatus
  + resolve(action : String)
}

class AccountType <<Enumeration>> {
  personal
  magazine
}
class Role <<Enumeration>> {
  reader
  writer
  admin
}
class Plan <<Enumeration>> {
  free
  premium
}
class ArticleStatus <<Enumeration>> {
  draft
  published
}
class Placement <<Enumeration>> {
  public
  marketplace
}
class Visibility <<Enumeration>> {
  free
  premium
}
class NotificationType <<Enumeration>> {
  follow
  like
  comment
  reply
  repost
  article_previewed
  article_purchased
  earnings_credited
  subscription_renewed
  comment_like
  save
  article_published
}
class ReportTargetType <<Enumeration>> {
  article
  user
  comment
}
class ReportStatus <<Enumeration>> {
  pending
  reviewed
  resolved
  dismissed
}

User "1" -- "0..1" MagazineProfile : extends
User "1" -- "0..*" Article : writes
User "0..1" -- "0..*" Article : publishes
User "1" -- "0..*" Comment : posts
User "1" -- "0..*" Notification : receives
User "0..1" -- "0..*" Report : files
Article "1" -- "0..*" Comment : carries
Comment "0..1" -- "0..*" Comment : replies to

User "0..*" -- "0..*" Article : likes
User "0..*" -- "0..*" Article : reposts
User "0..*" -- "0..*" Article : saves
User "0..*" -- "0..*" Comment : likes
User "0..*" -- "0..*" User : follows
User "0..*" -- "0..*" User : blocks
Article "0..*" -- "0..*" Tag : is tagged with

note as N1
  likes, reposts, saves, follows, blocks and comment
  likes are many-to-many associations: each is stored as
  a join table holding the pair and a date, with a
  unique constraint on the pair.
end note

note as N2
  role and plan are NULL for a magazine account,
  enforced by a CHECK constraint. They are
  orthogonal: a writer may stay on the free plan.
  publisherId names the magazine that published a
  licensed article; it is NULL for everything else.
end note

AccountType -[hidden]down- Role
Role -[hidden]down- Plan
ArticleStatus -[hidden]down- Placement
Placement -[hidden]down- Visibility
NotificationType -[hidden]down- ReportTargetType
ReportTargetType -[hidden]down- ReportStatus
AccountType -[hidden]right- ArticleStatus
ArticleStatus -[hidden]right- NotificationType
@enduml
